## Loading placeholders

### Full-screen / section loading (first paint)
Use skeleton widgets from the project's two placeholder locations:

- **Skeletons/shimmer:** `lib/utils/widgets/skeletons/` — contains `shimmer.dart`, `skeleton.dart`, `widgets.dart` (pre-built bones), `stylings.dart`, `theme.dart`.
- **Named placeholders:** `lib/utils/widgets/place_holders/` — contains ready-made feature-shaped placeholders:
  - `post_card_place_holder.dart`
  - `posts_place_holder.dart`
  - `followers_list_place_holder.dart`
  - `follower_place_holder.dart`
  - `profile_info_card_place_holder.dart`
  - `profile_count_view_card_place_holder.dart`
  - `reel_player_place_holder.dart`
  - `list_view_place_holder.dart`
  - `custom_list_tile_place_holder.dart`

Prefer reusing an existing named placeholder before building a new skeleton. When creating a new one, put it in `lib/utils/widgets/place_holders/` (shared) or `lib/src/<feature>/components/` (feature-specific). Mirror the real content layout — cards, list rows, primary actions — so the transition is smooth.

Do **not** use a centred `CircularProgressIndicator` for full-screen or section loads.

### Inline / button loading (small targets)
A compact spinner inside a button or OTP row is fine. These are not "page loads."

### Theme consistency
Use `colorScheme.surfaceContainerHighest` (or the closest project token from `lib/theme/app_theme.dart`) for skeleton bone colors so placeholders respect dark/light mode.

