## Bidirectional row layout (RTL / LTR)

- Follow `Directionality.of(context)` derived from the app locale. Do not set `textDirection` on a subtree based on string content.
- **Title or action cluster beside a badge:** in the LTR remaining space, align with `AlignmentDirectional.centerStart` so the cluster sits at the leading edge. Avoid `AlignmentDirectional.centerEnd` for that cluster in LTR — it pushes content to the trailing edge and mirrors RTL.
- **Badge vs expanded block:** if the badge must sit on the opposite physical side in RTL vs LTR, reorder `Row` children (e.g. `[badge, Expanded(...)]` for LTR, `[Expanded(...), badge]` for RTL) instead of using non-directional `left`/`right` alignment.
- **Two action buttons:** keep primary placement consistent with locale (LTR: `[secondary, primary]`; mirror for RTL when the design requires it).

---

## Theme and styling
- All colors and text styles must come from `lib/theme/app_theme.dart` tokens.
- Do not hardcode `TextStyle(...)`, `Color(0x...)`, or `Colors.*` literals in widget files.
- When a design value has no matching token: (1) map to the closest existing token, or (2) add a new semantic token to `app_theme.dart` (e.g. `cardBorderColor`, `sectionTitleStyle`), or (3) as a last resort hardcode with `// TODO: move to AppTheme`.
- Token names are semantic, not value-based: `successBackground` not `greenLight1`; `sectionTitleStyle` not `font14Bold`.
